Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: tcpm: no DR_Swap while a VDM is in progress

A Discover Identity or another VDM exchange is an interruptible AMS, so
tcpm_ams_start() lets a DATA_ROLE_SWAP begin while the port still waits
for the VDM's reply.  That reply is on its way by then.  It collides with
the DR_Swap, which the TCPC reports as discarded, and is received in
DR_SWAP_SEND.  The swap cannot be interrupted, and at PD 3.x
tcpm_pd_handle_msg() answers the reply with a Soft Reset.

On the SM-X910 a "host" written to the port's data_role 3.6 ms after
SNK_READY, 0.5 ms after the Discover Identity had gone out, ended that
way:

  AMS DISCOVER_IDENTITY start
  PD TX complete, status: 0
  AMS DATA_ROLE_SWAP start
  state change AMS_START -> DR_SWAP_SEND [rev3 DATA_ROLE_SWAP]
  PD TX complete, status: 1
  PD RX, header: 0x57af [1]
  state change DR_SWAP_SEND -> SNK_SOFT_RESET [rev3 DATA_ROLE_SWAP]

The contract was negotiated again and the swap was not sent a second
time.

Refuse the DATA_ROLE_SWAP with -EAGAIN while the VDM state machine runs.
That is the test tcpm_send_discover_work() and tcpm_enable_frs_work() use
for an idle port.  tcpm_dr_set() hands the error to userspace, which can
write again.  The request for DFP before discovery waits for the VDM
state machine itself and never gets here with it running.  A swap the
partner asks for does not come through tcpm_ams_start() and is handled as
before.
---
 drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c b/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c
@@ -1700,6 +1700,17 @@ static int tcpm_ams_start(struct tcpm_po
 		return -EAGAIN;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * A VDM exchange may be interrupted, a DR_Swap may not.  A DR_Swap
+	 * that is sent while a VDM waits for its reply gets that reply as its
+	 * answer, which ends in a Soft Reset.  The requester can try again.
+	 */
+	if (ams == DATA_ROLE_SWAP && port->vdm_sm_running) {
+		port->upcoming_state = INVALID_STATE;
+		tcpm_log(port, "VDM in progress, DATA_ROLE_SWAP not started");
+		return -EAGAIN;
+	}
+
 	if (port->pwr_role == TYPEC_SOURCE) {
 		enum typec_cc_status cc_req = port->cc_req;
 
